      "cells": {
        "rest": {
          "ok": true,
          "ms": 9979,
          "value": "`deno_core` is a Rust crate that serves as the essential bridge between Rust and the V8 JavaScript engine, providing the core JavaScript runtime (`JsRuntime`) and the infrastructure for defining native operations (ops) callable from JavaScript within Deno.   \n\n## Notes\nThe `deno_core` crate is located in `libs/core/`  and is a fundamental part of Deno's layered architecture.  It handles the execution of JavaScript, manages an event loop, and allows Rust functions to be exposed to JavaScript as \"ops\" using the `deno_core::extension!` macro. \n\nWiki pages you might want to explore:\n- [Deno Overview (denoland/deno)](/wiki/denoland/deno#1)\n\nView this search on DeepWiki: https://deepwiki.com/search/in-one-sentence-what-is-denoco_23dfde44-6d02-4cc0-a959-80bfbb7664aa\n"
        },
        "graphql": {
          "ok": true,
          "ms": 9839,
          "value": "`deno_core` is a Rust crate that serves as the essential bridge between Deno's Rust-based runtime and the V8 JavaScript engine, providing core functionalities like the `JsRuntime` for executing JavaScript and a system for registering native Rust functions as \"ops\" callable from JavaScript. \n\nWiki pages you might want to explore:\n- [Deno Overview (denoland/deno)](/wiki/denoland/deno#1)\n\nView this search on DeepWiki: https://deepwiki.com/search/in-one-sentence-what-is-denoco_ac0e4d77-e524-4a8d-8a2a-87fafde663f9\n"
        },
        "mcp": {
          "ok": true,
          "ms": 10027,
          "value": "`deno_core` is a Rust crate that serves as the core JavaScript runtime bridge for Deno, providing essential V8 bindings and an event loop abstraction to execute JavaScript code. \n\n## Notes\nThe provided context indicates that `deno_core` is a fundamental component within the Deno architecture, acting as the bridge between Rust and the V8 JavaScript engine.  It is located in the `libs/core/` directory  and is a dependency for many other Deno extensions, such as `deno_ffi`, `deno_fs`, `deno_io`, `deno_node`, and `deno_os`. \n\nWiki pages you might want to explore:\n- [Deno Overview (denoland/deno)](/wiki/denoland/deno#1)\n\nView this search on DeepWiki: https://deepwiki.com/search/in-one-sentence-what-is-denoco_dfc175ad-9805-4f2d-aa1c-b9f84c6c3860\n"
        }
      }
